					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12767505#post-4413298</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12767505/death-perception#post-4413298</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 02 Nov 2019 23:57:41 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Pedantique</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3118444</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This tale strikes a very natural balance between its humorous and melancholy elements that is rare on the site. The clash between the general tragedy that feels inherent to Samsara's members doesn't overwhelm the childish confusion and glee, and the somewhat alien perspective highlights the absurdity of Halloween's weird traditions. The dialogue's good, nothing overstays its welcome, and I'm persistently amused by the howled Spice Girls song. Easiest +1 I've given in a while.</p> <p>(I think I do like some of the other possible titles better though.)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
